<?xml version="1.0"?>
<CP_Scriptfile date="Feb 19, 2023">
<CPscript title="Conformal Welding" level="min" screenmode="map" >
<description>Weld two owls together, windtip on one to a boundary circle you choose on the other. The result of the welding gives a triangulation of the sphere; this is packed and displayed, with the 'eyes' of the two owls and the welding seem showing.</description>
<text> Here's your friendly owl, with a wingtip marked, along with a reverse oriented doppelganger. </text>
<cmd name="*" mnemonic="*" tooltip="Start over" iconname="editdelete.png">act 0;Cleanse;Map 0 1;infile_read Owl.p;color -c 20 21 22;color -c 209 54;Disp -w -c -cf 21 22 54;copy 1;reorient -p1;layout -p1;Disp -p1 -w -c -cf 21 22;set_Elist b; </cmd>
<text> Press 'x' to choose a yellow boundary vertex in p1. Then press 'w' to carry out the welding. (This is like pasting the yellow circles of the two packings to one another, then continuing to paste clockwise around one boundary and counterclockwise around the other, until the full boundaries have been identified.) The result is a sphere and its max packing appears in p2. Start over and try some other points.

The red curve on the sphere, the join line between the two packings, is called the "welding curve". The simplest is an equator, which results if you mark the wingtip of p1 which is pointing towards p0 (vertex 54). A similar result is obtained from p0 alone with the 'double' command. See the meaning in "Help".

You can use this same setup with minor alterations with other packings. You can even weld different packings, the only requirement being that they have the same number of boundary vertices. </text>
<Section title="Tools">
<cmd inline="no" name="x" mnemonic="x" tooltip="choose a boundary circle in p1" iconname="kghostview.png" dropable="yes">set_vlist -p1 z #XY;mark -p1 -cw -c vlist;set_vlist -p1 {c:(m).and.(b)};Disp -p1 -cf vlist;set_Vlist 54 vlist;color -p1 -c 209 Vlist[1];disp -p0 -w -c -cf 21 22 54;Disp -p1 -w -c -cf 21 22 Vlist[1]; </cmd>
<cmd name="w" mnemonic="w" tooltip="do the welding and display the resulting sphere" iconname="amarok.png">act 2;copy -p1 2;set_screen -d;set_elist b;adjoin 2 0 Vlist[1] 54 -1;max_pack -p2;color -p2 -c 100 a;color -p2 -c 20 {c:d.gt.12};color -p2 -c 209 54;Disp -p2 -w -cf -et4c180 Elist;Map 0 2; </cmd>
</Section>
  </CPscript>
